  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **Phase 3: Metrics - Quantifying ICL Performance**\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Three Complementary Metrics**\n",
    "\n",
    "We measure ICL using three different but related metrics:\n",
    "\n",
    "### **📊 Metric 1: Cross-Entropy Loss**\n",
    "**Formula**: `-log P_model(true_next_digit)`  \n",
    "**Interpretation**: Model's prediction accuracy - lower is better  \n",
    "**ICL Evidence**: Should **decrease** with position for learnable patterns  \n",
    "\n",
    "### **🎯 Metric 2: KL Divergence to Bayesian Optimal**\n",
    "**Formula**: `KL(P_bayesian || P_model)`  \n",
    "**Interpretation**: How far is the model from theoretically perfect performance?  \n",
    "**ICL Evidence**: Should **decrease** as model approaches optimal predictor  \n",
    "\n",
    "### **🔍 Metric 3: KL Divergence from Uniform**  \n",
    "**Formula**: `KL(P_model || P_uniform)`  \n",
    "**Interpretation**: How much \"information\" has the model gained?  \n",
    "**ICL Evidence**: Should **increase** as model learns patterns (moves away from uniform guessing)\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Why Three Metrics?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Each captures different aspects of learning:\n",
    "- **Cross-entropy**: Practical performance \n",
    "- **KL to Bayesian**: Optimality gap\n",
    "- **KL from uniform**: Information accumulation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Convergent evidence**: True ICL should show consistent patterns across all three metrics.\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Position-wise Analysis**\n",
    "\n",
    "We compute metrics at each sequence position and average across sequences:\n",
    "- **Position 1**: Model has seen 1 token, predicting token 2\n",
    "- **Position 50**: Model has seen 50 tokens, predicting token 51  \n",
    "- **Position 149**: Model has seen 149 tokens, predicting token 150\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected patterns**:\n",
    "- **Uniform DGP**: Flat lines (no learning possible)\n",
    "- **Multinomial DGP**: Improving performance over time  \n",
    "- **Random Walk**: Rapid initial learning, then plateau\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "✅ Metrics computation functions defined\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Phase 3: Metrics Computation Functions\n",
    "def compute_cross_entropy_loss(model_dist, true_token):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute cross-entropy loss: -log P_model(true_token)\"\"\"\n",
    "    epsilon = 1e-10  # For numerical stability\n",
    "    return -np.log(model_dist[true_token] + epsilon)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_kl_divergence(p, q):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute KL(p || q) = sum p * log(p/q)\"\"\"\n",
    "    epsilon = 1e-10  # For numerical stability\n",
    "    p = np.array(p) + epsilon\n",
    "    q = np.array(q) + epsilon\n",
    "    return np.sum(p * np.log(p / q))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_metrics_for_dgp(dgp_name, sequences, bayesian_optimal, model_results):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute all metrics for a given DGP\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nComputing metrics for {dgp_name}...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    model_distributions = model_results[\"model_distributions\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Initialize metric storage\n",
    "    cross_entropy_losses = []  # List of lists (sequence x position)\n",
    "    kl_to_bayesian = []  # List of lists (sequence x position)\n",
    "    kl_from_uniform = []  # List of lists (sequence x position)\n",
    "\n",
    "    uniform_dist = np.full(K, 1.0 / K)  # Uniform distribution for reference\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Process each sequence\n",
    "    for seq_idx, (sequence, seq_bayesian, seq_model_dists) in enumerate(\n",
    "        zip(sequences, bayesian_optimal, model_distributions)\n",
    "    ):\n",
    "        seq_ce_losses = []\n",
    "        seq_kl_bayes = []\n",
    "        seq_kl_uniform = []\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Process each position in the sequence\n",
    "        for pos_idx, (model_dist, bayes_dist) in enumerate(\n",
    "            zip(seq_model_dists, seq_bayesian[: len(seq_model_dists)])\n",
    "        ):\n",
    "            if pos_idx + 1 < len(sequence):  # Make sure we have a true next token\n",
    "                true_next_token = sequence[pos_idx + 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "                # Metric 1: Cross-entropy loss\n",
    "                ce_loss = compute_cross_entropy_loss(model_dist, true_next_token)\n",
    "                seq_ce_losses.append(ce_loss)\n",
    "\n",
    "                # Metric 2: KL divergence to Bayesian optimal\n",
    "                kl_bayes = compute_kl_divergence(bayes_dist, model_dist)\n",
    "                seq_kl_bayes.append(kl_bayes)\n",
    "\n",
    "                # Metric 3: KL divergence from uniform (information gained)\n",
    "                kl_uniform = compute_kl_divergence(model_dist, uniform_dist)\n",
    "                seq_kl_uniform.append(kl_uniform)\n",
    "\n",
    "        cross_entropy_losses.append(seq_ce_losses)\n",
    "        kl_to_bayesian.append(seq_kl_bayes)\n",
    "        kl_from_uniform.append(seq_kl_uniform)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Average metrics across sequences at each position\n",
    "    max_length = max(len(seq) for seq in cross_entropy_losses)\n",
    "\n",
    "    avg_ce_loss = []\n",
    "    avg_kl_bayes = []\n",
    "    avg_kl_uniform = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for pos in range(max_length):\n",
    "        # Collect values at this position across all sequences\n",
    "        pos_ce_losses = [seq[pos] for seq in cross_entropy_losses if len(seq) > pos]\n",
    "        pos_kl_bayes = [seq[pos] for seq in kl_to_bayesian if len(seq) > pos]\n",
    "        pos_kl_uniform = [seq[pos] for seq in kl_from_uniform if len(seq) > pos]\n",
    "\n",
    "        if pos_ce_losses:  # If we have data at this position\n",
    "            avg_ce_loss.append(np.mean(pos_ce_losses))\n",
    "            avg_kl_bayes.append(np.mean(pos_kl_bayes))\n",
    "            avg_kl_uniform.append(np.mean(pos_kl_uniform))\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"cross_entropy_loss\": avg_ce_loss,\n",
    "        \"kl_to_bayesian\": avg_kl_bayes,\n",
    "        \"kl_from_uniform\": avg_kl_uniform,\n",
    "        \"positions\": list(range(len(avg_ce_loss))),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Metrics computation functions defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
