    "## **Phase 5: Results**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Experimental Design**: 3 DGPs (uniform control, multinomial bias, random walk), 200 sequences × 150 tokens each, compared to Bayesian optimal baselines\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Findings**:\n",
    "1. **Task-dependent learning**: ICL occurs only for learnable patterns (multinomial, random walk), not uniform control\n",
    "2. **Systematic improvement**: Cross-entropy loss decreases, approaches Bayesian optimal over time\n",
    "3. **Pattern-appropriate dynamics**: Different learning rates match task structure\n",
    "\n",
    "**Evidence for genuine ICL**:\n",
    "- ✅ No spurious learning on uniform data (control works)\n",
    "- ✅ Clear learning curves for structured data  \n",
    "- ✅ Approaches but doesn't reach theoretical optimum\n",
    "- ✅ Task-specific learning rates (gradual for multinomial, rapid for random walk)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Conclusion**: GPT-2 exhibits systematic, task-dependent approximate Bayesian inference - the hallmarks of genuine in-context learning.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **This Study Demonstrates:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **🎯 ICL is Task-Dependent**: Model exhibits learning only when learnable patterns exist\n",
    "2. **📈 Systematic Inference**: GPT-2 performs approximate Bayesian inference, not memorization  \n",
    "3. **⚡ Context Sensitivity**: Performance improvements correlate with sequence structure\n",
    "4. **🔍 Genuine Learning**: Results distinguish ICL from pattern matching or retrieval\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **Scientific Significance:**\n",
